格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A terminal coding interface that brings the DeepSeek Harness kernel's full capability set — special modes, plugins, model & subagent management — to the terminal. Interaction layer inspired by Claude Code, Codex CLI, and Pi agent; model-switch animations; unified panel key gramma","id":"gh:1333936445","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-code","slug":"UNLINEARITY/dsh-code","topics":["agent","ai-coding","ai-terminal","claude-code","cli","codex","coding-assistant","deepseek","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","harness","ink","llm","plugin","react","terminal","tui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A terminal coding interface that brings the DeepSeek Harness kernel's full capability set — special "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"modes, plugins, model & subagent management — to the terminal. Interaction layer inspired by Claude "},{"id":"p1s3","text":"Code, Codex CLI, and Pi agent; model-switch animations; unified panel key gramma"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# DSH-Code"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## 1. Project overview"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**DSH-Code is a terminal coding interface for DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`).** It is composed as an out-o"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"f-tree bundle on top of the official `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base` and uses the same Agent, Session, tool,"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" command, skill, permission, sandbox, context-compaction, and plugin services as the Harness Web UI."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness registers models, tools, storage, policies, and interfaces as plugins through Cordi"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"s. Durable session events record the information required to restore conversations and runtime state"},{"id":"p6s3","text":". DSH-Code preserves that architecture while adding a terminal workflow suited to coding tasks. The "},{"id":"p6s4","text":"interface follows terminal conventions familiar to developers, while runtime behavior remains govern"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"ed by DSH services and configuration."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## 2. Quick start"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"2.1.0 release notes"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Requires Node `>=24.9.0` and the preview `dsh` CLI (current release line: `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-rc"},{"id":"p9s2","text":".1`). You can still enter the TUI, browse sessions, and use non-model features without configuring a"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" model; press `Tab` in `/model` to manage API keys, OAuth, device-code sign-in, endpoints, and model"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"odel; press `Tab` in `/model` to manage API keys, OAuth, device-code sign-in, endpoints, and models."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### 1. Install and update"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The commands below install the published `dsh-code@2.1.0` with its matching Harness version. This ch"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"eckout targets Harness `0.2.2-rc.1`; use the source installation below for this checkout. Close all "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"running `dsh` / `deepseek` sessions before installing or upgrading."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Use `/update` or `deepseek update --apply` for later updates. See installation and upgrade troublesh"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"ooting for version alignment, dependency repair, and migration errors."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### 2. Launch commands"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Available launch commands:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"`dsh --profile cli`, `deepseek`, and `dsh-code` are equivalent launch commands. `deepseek` and `dsh-"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"code` are global aliases for `dsh --profile cli`, and all additional arguments are forwarded unchang"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ed, for example `deepseek --resume abc123`."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> DeepSeek Harness is still a developer preview and may introduce compatibility-breaking changes. DS"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"H-Code will continue to track the evolution of its plugin interfaces."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## 3. Core features and usage"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"DSH-Code brings DSH Agents, models, tools, and durable sessions directly into the terminal, covering"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" the complete workflow from writing code to reviewing changes."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### 1. Session management"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- Create sessions with `/new`, or restore existing sessions with `/resume` and `--continue`\n- Create"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" a new work branch from a historical point with `/fork` while preserving the original session\n- Sear"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ch history by current directory, update time, and session scope\n- Recall input history with Up/Down "},{"id":"p22s4","text":"(typed slash commands included), or search previous prompts and commands with `/history`\n- Use persi"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"stent titles, Markdown export, context occupancy, token, cache, TTFT, and elapsed-time metrics; `/us"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"age` reports the harness token meter's four disjoint buckets, the totals merged by model, and a per-"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"turn breakdown\n- The status bar's `in` counts only uncached input, and `cache` shows both the cache-"},{"id":"p22s8","text":"read volume and the hit share — together they are the billed prompt side\n- Restore the session's Age"},{"id":"p22s9","text":"nt Preset, model selection, and subagent list when resuming it; the welcome header shows both the ds"},{"id":"p22s10","text":"h and dsh-code versions"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"### 2. Agents, models, and extensions"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"- Select an independent Agent Preset for each session to compose tools, prompt sections, skills, con"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"text compaction, plan mode, and subagent capabilities\n- Use `/mode` to select `standard`, `ptc`, `mi"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"nimal`, `cordis`, or a user-defined Preset (the legacy `code` id maps to `ptc`)\n- Use `/model` to sw"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"itch models and manage providers, API keys, OAuth/device-code sign-in, endpoints, available models, "},{"id":"p24s5","text":"and context windows\n- In the `/model` provider list, Enter manages a manual API key, `l` starts sign"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"-in, and `o` logs out after confirmation\n- Automatically load commands and skills available in DSH; "},{"id":"p24s7","text":"use `/help` to find them and `/plugin` to inspect extension status\n- Use plans, goals, todos, permis"},{"id":"p24s8","text":"sions, sandboxes, subagents, and additional instructions while a task is running"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### 3. Model-switch animations"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The composer plays Wave, Aurora, or Pulse when the model or reasoning effort changes under the follo"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"ys Wave, Aurora, or Pulse when the model or reasoning effort changes under the following conditions:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| Scenario | Trigger | Animation text | Effect tier |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Official DeepSeek model | Switch to the model, or change its reasoning effort | `deepseek` | Flash"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" uses the single-band tier; other DeepSeek models use the multi-band tier |\n| Other models | After c"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"hanging the model or reasoning effort, the effective effort is strictly above `high` | `Into the Unk"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"nown` | Uses the same multi-band tier as non-Flash DeepSeek models |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Levels above `high` include `xhigh`, `x-high`, `very-high`, `max`, `maximum`, and `ultra`. For non-D"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"eepSeek models, `high`, `medium`, `low`, and `off` do not trigger an animation."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"| Style | Flash | Other DeepSeek / `Into the Unknown` |"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"| Wave | One blue crest sweeps from left to right, about 1.2 seconds | Two offset blue crests sweep "},{"id":"p31s2","text":"across in sequence with trailing `· ✦ ✧` sparkles, about 1.5 seconds |\n| Aurora | Two blue light ban"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ds drift across one another, about 1.5 seconds | Three differently hued light bands drift across one"},{"id":"p31s4","text":" another, about 1.8 seconds |\n| Pulse | One ring expands outward from the center of the composer, ab"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"out 1.1 seconds | Two rings expand outward in sequence, about 1.45 seconds |"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"`/animation off` disables purely decorative effects such as Wave/Pulse, animated theme flow, and rai"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"nbow bursts. The input cursor, streaming caret, busy chase, Thinking/Deep Diving shimmer, and `Deep "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"diving...` clock remain live so an active turn never looks frozen."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
